[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Start "giuoco-main 3.Bc4"]
[Name "Two Knights Defence: the quiet 4.d3"]

3... Nf6 { The Two Knights Defence: instead of copying with ...Bc5, Black develops the other knight with an attack on e4. [%cal Rf6e4] }
4. d3 { Guards e4 and keeps the game quiet, in the same style as the main line. 4.Ng5 attacks f7 at once, but after 4...d5 it asks for a run of exact moves on both sides; 4.d3 is the engine's choice too and needs none. [%cal Gd3e4] }
4... Bc5 { Black's most common answer: the bishop goes to its best square, aiming at f2 as in the Giuoco Piano. }
5. c3 { Prepares d4. This is now the main line's position, reached in a different order: everything learned there applies from here. [%cal Gc3d4] } *
